TITLE:: Polivoks
summary:: Virtual Analog Model of the Formanta Polivoks VCF
categories:: UGens>Filters
related:: Classes/FSWasp, Classes/FSSteiner, Classes/MS20Diode

DESCRIPTION::
Polivoks is a virtual analog model of the legendary voltage-controlled filter designed by Vladimir Kuzmin in 1982 for the Soviet Formanta Polivoks synthesizer.

The Polivoks VCF is an idiosyncratic state-variable integrator cascade built using two Soviet K140UD12 (К140УД12 / µA776 equivalent) programmable operational amplifiers. In this classic Soviet circuit, no external capacitors are used in the core integrators; instead, dynamic control of the op-amp programming current (I_set) modulates the internal slew rate and transconductance to sweep the cutoff frequency.

Stage P1 implements the linearized two-stage integrator cascade with exact bilinear prewarped tuning and analytical damping. It provides switchable Low-Pass (LP, 12 dB/octave) and Band-Pass (BP, 6 dB/octave) modes, faithfully reproducing the two native physical responses of the original hardware.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar

ARGUMENT:: in
Audio-rate input signal.

ARGUMENT:: freq
Filter cutoff frequency in Hertz (10 Hz to 0.49 * sampleRate). Supports audio-rate (.ar) and control-rate (.kr) modulation.

ARGUMENT:: res
Resonance parameter in [0.0, 1.0], mapping to the feedback damping factor r in [2.0, 0.02].
At res = 0.0, the filter is critically damped (Q = 0.5).
At res = 1.0, the filter exhibits intense resonant peaking (Q = 50.0).

ARGUMENT:: mode
Filter mode selection (integer, init-only):
TABLE::
## 0 || Low-Pass (12 dB/octave roll-off)
## 1 || Band-Pass (symmetric 6 dB/octave skirts)
::
(Note: The Formanta Polivoks hardware does not provide a High-Pass mode; only LP and BP are supported).

ARGUMENT:: drive
Input drive scaling factor (default 1.0).

returns:: An audio-rate filtered signal.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
// Boot server
s.boot;

// 1. Low-Pass sweep with saw oscillator
(
x = {
    var src = Saw.ar([110, 110.5]) * 0.2;
    var cutoff = SinOsc.kr(0.2).exprange(100, 8000);
    Polivoks.ar(src, freq: cutoff, res: 0.6, mode: 0, drive: 1.0) * 0.3;
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 2. Band-Pass noise sweep with screaming resonance
(
x = {
    var src = PinkNoise.ar(0.3 ! 2);
    var cutoff = SinOsc.kr(0.15).exprange(200, 4000);
    Polivoks.ar(src, freq: cutoff, res: 0.85, mode: 1, drive: 1.0) * 0.4;
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 3. Audio-rate FM modulation
(
x = {
    var mod = SinOsc.ar(150) * 1200;
    var cutoff = (2000 + mod).clip(20, 18000);
    var src = Pulse.ar(55, 0.3) * 0.25 ! 2;
    Polivoks.ar(src, freq: cutoff, res: 0.7, mode: 0, drive: 1.0) * 0.3;
}.play;
)
x.free;
::
